    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The build passes with all tests (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `selfLink` field so the Owner response returns `/api/owners/` followed by the owner id.\n\nThe DTOs are generated from the OpenAPI spec, and derived read-only fields are populated via MapStruct expressions, so I followed that existing convention:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `selfLink` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (right after `id`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `selfLink` field with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(selfLink(owner))\")` and a `selfLink(Owner)` default method that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (null when the owner has no id yet).\n\nBecause the mapper is used on both the create (`addOwner`) and read (`getOwner`) paths, the field is populated consistently. The acceptance test `coreReturnsSelfLink` \u2014 which creates an owner then GETs it and asserts `$.selfLink == \"/api/owners/\" + id` \u2014 passes.",
